      "content": "i see. so you're basically saying retribution is just \"vengeance\" while restorative justice is \"ethical.\" if someone's argument is that punishment is a necessary moral duty to uphold the law and provide justice for the victim, you're still framing that as just a \"desire for vengeance\" rather than a legitimate moral principle? isn't that a bit one-sided?",
